{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 5, :comments ["<b>And she bore Jacob a son.</b> In the case of all the handmaids Scripture mentions \"to Jacob,\" to indicate that he desired them and acknowledged them, and they are not called the son of the handmaid but rather a son to Jacob, like the sons of the mistresses who trace their lineage to him. And concerning Leah it says a fifth son and a sixth son \"to Jacob,\" because of the multiplication of sons, to say that in all of them he delights and all of them he brings near, but concerning the earlier ones it did not say thus:"], :book :genesis, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:36:38.243597728Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}